sequenceDiagram
  actor P as Person
  participant B as Board card (React view)
  participant H as Host (Claude, ChatGPT, ...)
  participant A as Assistant
  participant S as Game server (Hono)
  P->>B: clicks row 1, column 2
  B->>H: play_move(X, expectedMoveNumber 0)
  H->>S: play_move
  S-->>H: game, move 1
  H-->>B: result to the calling action (onSuccess)
  B->>B: show X, squares disabled
  alt game in progress, O next
    B->>H: appendMessage("Your move in game ...", context: game)
    Note over B,H: ui/update-model-context, then ui/message
    H->>A: the person's message, with the game as context
    opt context missing
      A->>H: get_game
      H->>S: get_game
      S-->>H: game, move 1
      H-->>A: result
    end
    A->>H: play_move(O, expectedMoveNumber 1)
    H->>S: play_move
    S-->>H: game, move 2
    H-->>A: result (no card opened)
    loop bounded wait, about every 1.5 s
      B->>H: get_game
      H->>S: get_game
      S-->>H: game, move 2
      H-->>B: result to the waiting board
    end
    B->>B: show O, squares enabled for X
  else X won, or the board is full
    B->>H: appendMessage("I won our tic-tac-toe game.")
    H->>A: the person's message (no move asked)
  end
  Note over B,S: A late append result is ignored unless the board still shows the same game and move.<br/>A stale card or repeated request sends an old expectedMoveNumber, which the server refuses with no effect.
